<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
  <!--
    The time data home's generator (milestone SJL-8.2; Broiler.VM's decision JSD-0076, decisions
    SJL-D-1 (b-iii), SJL-D-6 (c), SJL-D-20 and SJL-D-21): the readers of the pinned tz archive, the
    CLDR time zone keys and the calendar crates, the tz compiler, and the generators of the compact
    time zone tables and the calendar year table, ported from Broiler.VM's architecture tests with
    their behaviour unchanged. Each generator is split into its data - the bytes and text an engine
    embeds - and a source writer that wraps that data into a C# file for a namespace and class the
    caller chooses, as Broiler.Unicode.Generation's UnicodeTableGenerator and UnicodeTableSource are.

    It is test-only in the way that package is: each engine's tests call it to regenerate the tables
    that engine embeds and hold them byte for byte, and it never reaches a product closure. It reads
    no file itself: the caller hands it each pin's text and each archive's bytes. It carries no
    table and no pinned input (SJL-D-6 (c)): those are files of this repository, under
    Broiler.ECMAScript/data/time/, never package content.

    Milestone SJL-9.2b (Broiler.VM's decision JSD-0082, decisions D10-D12) adds the Intl data home's
    generator in Intl/: the CLDR and UCD pin readers, the reader of the UCD subset the collation tables
    need, and the generator of the Intl and collation tables, ported from Broiler.VM's architecture
    tests, with the locales, numbering-system symbols, calendars and tailorings as parameters. With
    Broiler.VM's parameters it writes Broiler.VM's JsCldrTables.g.cs byte for byte; its pinned inputs
    and Broiler.JS's tables are files under Broiler.ECMAScript/data/intl/, never package content.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation</AssemblyName>
    <PackageId>Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation</PackageId>
    <Description>Test-only: the generator of the Broiler JavaScript engines' time zone, calendar and Intl tables from the pinned IANA tz release, CLDR's time zone keys, ICU4X's calendar crates, CLDR's JSON data and the Unicode Character Database - the pin readers, a tz compiler equivalent to zic, the compact zone, identifier and region tables, the calendar year table, the Intl and collation tables, and writers that wrap them into C# or raw files - for engines that embed the tables and hold them byte for byte. It carries no table and no pinned input.</Description>
    <PackageTags>broiler;ecmascript;javascript;shared;generator;tzdb;calendars;cldr;intl;test</PackageTags>
    <EnablePackageValidation>true</EnablePackageValidation>
  </PropertyGroup>
  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The tests call the compiler's internal steps (the ON-field and rule-event readers) directly. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Broiler.ECMAScript.Generation.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
